    def: 'What earns a memory write — and what is allowed to fade.',
    insight: 'The write gate is the quality control for every future retrieval. Write too much and search drowns; decay is how wrong memories stop being permanent.',
    failure: 'Write-everything, forget-nothing: a year later, retrieval surfaces confident notes from a codebase that no longer exists.',
